## Per-field rationale (`provenance`) — ALWAYS emit, as an ARRAY

Emit a `provenance` **array** on each `specimen_findings` record — ONE entry per
field you populated in THAT record. Each entry is
`{field_name, block_id, page, type, rationale}` where `field_name` is the populated
field, `type` is one of `verbatim` | `inferred` | `derived` | `absent`, and
`rationale` is ONE short clause saying WHY you chose that value (required when
`type` is `inferred`/`derived`). This is the per-field "why" the SME reviewer reads —
emit it for EVERY field you populated, keep it brief, ground it in a cited block,
and never restate PHI beyond the value itself. Use an ARRAY (not a keyed object).

```json
"provenance": [
  { "field_name": "tissue_type", "block_id": "b12", "page": 1, "type": "verbatim",
    "rationale": "specimen header reads 'Breast, left, core biopsy'" },
  { "field_name": "pTNM_stage", "block_id": "b30", "page": 2, "type": "inferred",
    "rationale": "stage assembled from the synoptic T and N rows" }
]
```

Now run the ReAct loop and produce the `significant_findings` object — one
`specimen_findings` entry per specimen, each fully mapped. Emit
`specimen_findings: []` if there is no surgical-pathology content.
